Subject: [PATCH] alsa: drain the PCM before closing it for a rate or format change

When the sample rate or format changes, the output thread closes the PCM
with snd_pcm_close() without draining it: the last part of the previous
track still queued in the ALSA ring (400 ms with the default buffer) is
discarded, so the tail of a 44.1 kHz track disappears when the next one is
96 kHz.

Before reopening for a new format or rate, wait for snd_pcm_drain() to
finish, so the tail is played. The wait is bounded by the real buffer
duration plus 100 ms (at most 1 s) and never blocks the output lock. If the
player is stopped or switched off while waiting, or the drain does not
complete in time, fall back to the immediate snd_pcm_drop(). User stop and
pause paths are unchanged. Nothing changes when the format is the same.

Source: local change
Upstream: Not submitted (local option)

--- a/output_alsa.c
+++ b/output_alsa.c
@@ -265,6 +265,39 @@
 	return NULL;
 }
 
+// Chiusura per cambio di formato o frequenza: prima di chiudere si lascia
+// uscire dal buffer ALSA la coda del brano appena finito, altrimenti
+// snd_pcm_close la scarta (con 400 ms di buffer sparivano le ultime centinaia
+// di ms). L'attesa e' limitata alla durata del buffer piu' un margine; se
+// l'utente ferma il player (stop) o l'uscita si spegne, o il drain non
+// finisce in tempo, si ripiega sul drop immediato.
+static void alsa_drain_before_close(void) {
+	unsigned limit_ms, waited_ms = 0;
+	int err;
+	if (!pcmp || !alsa.rate) return;
+	limit_ms = (unsigned)((unsigned long long)alsa.buffer_size * 1000 / alsa.rate) + 100;
+	if (limit_ms > 1000) limit_ms = 1000;
+	snd_pcm_nonblock(pcmp, 1);
+	while (running) {
+		bool stopped;
+		LOCK;
+		stopped = (output.state == OUTPUT_OFF || output.state == OUTPUT_STOPPED);
+		UNLOCK;
+		if (stopped) break;
+		err = snd_pcm_drain(pcmp);
+		if (err != -EAGAIN) {
+			if (err < 0) LOG_INFO("snd_pcm_drain error: %s", snd_strerror(err));
+			else LOG_INFO("drained %u ms before closing", waited_ms);
+			return;
+		}
+		if (waited_ms >= limit_ms) break;
+		usleep(5000);
+		waited_ms += 5;
+	}
+	LOG_INFO("drain skipped or timed out after %u ms: dropping", waited_ms);
+	snd_pcm_drop(pcmp);
+}
+
 static void alsa_close(void) {
 	int err;
 	if ((err = snd_pcm_close(pcmp)) < 0) {
@@ -689,6 +722,8 @@
 				relay_script(1);
 			}
 #endif
+			// cambio di formato o frequenza: la coda del brano precedente esce prima della chiusura
+			if (pcmp) alsa_drain_before_close();
 			LOG_INFO("open output device: %s", output.device);
 			LOCK;
 
